    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"Edgecase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.layout_random - Edgecase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"Edgecase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.layout_random.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.layout_random()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | Edgecase\n  description: Scatter the nodes uniformly at random over a square.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.layout_random()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | Edgecase\n  description: Scatter the nodes uniformly at random over a square.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.layout_random()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Scatter the nodes uniformly at random over a square.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nScatter the nodes uniformly at random over a square.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L5038-L5115){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.layout_random(\n    scale=1.0,\n    center=(0.0, 0.0),\n    seed=None,\n    attr_name=None,\n    return_dict=False,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Random layout](/assets/graphs/layout-random.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"On the left, a ring of eight nodes with two chords, drawn on a circle. On the right, layout_random(seed=71) drops each node at a uniformly random point in a square, ignoring the edges, so the ring is scrambled.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nEach coordinate is drawn independently and uniformly from\n`[center - scale, center + scale)`. Edges play no part. A random layout is a baseline\nto compare other layouts against, and a starting point for the iterative layouts via\ntheir `initial=` argument. Unlike NetworkX's `random_layout()`, which always uses the\nunit square `[0, 1)^2` shifted by `center`, the square here is `scale=`-sized and\ncentered, like the other layouts.\n\nPositions are stored as `[x, y]` lists in the `attr_name=` node attribute; see\n`layout_circular()`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[scale]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[1.0]{.fl}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Half the side of the square. Default is `1.0`.\n\n<code>[center]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [tuple[float, float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [(0.0, 0.0)]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Center of the square, as `(x, y)`. Default is the origin.\n\n<code>[seed]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[int]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Integer seed for the random number generator. The same `seed=` always gives the\n    same positions. If `None` (default), the positions differ on every call.\n\n<code>[attr_name]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Node attribute to store the positions in. If `None` (default), uses `\"pos\"`.\n\n<code>[return_dict]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, returns a dictionary instead of self. If `False` (default), stores the\n    positions on the nodes and returns self for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Union[dict[int, tuple[float, float]], Graph]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `return_dict=` is `True`: dictionary mapping node IDs to `(x, y)` tuples. If\n    `return_dict=` is `False` (default): returns self for method chaining.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `scale=` is not a positive number or `center=` is not a pair of numbers.\n:::\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nEvery coordinate falls within `scale=` of the center:\n\n::: {#0ba349f9 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\npos = ec.Graph().add_path_graph(100).layout_random(seed=3, return_dict=True)\n\nmax(max(abs(x), abs(y)) for x, y in pos.values()) <= 1\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\nTrue\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#a19aa827 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nec.Graph().add_grid_graph([5, 5]).layout_random(seed=3).plot(layout=\"pos\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"position:relative;display:inline-block\">\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"600\" height=\"400\" viewBox=\"103.2 9.8 399.8 394.9\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"103.2\" y=\"9.8\" width=\"399.8\" h